{"t":"panel","id":"ratio-note","title":"How seven speeds work","body":"The smallest rear sprocket gives a high gear for speed; the largest gives a low gear for climbing. Each shifter click changes the derailleur cable length enough to align the chain with the next sprocket.","anchor":"drivetrain"}
{"t":"panel","id":"freewheel-note","title":"Why it can coast","body":"A ratchet inside the rear freewheel lets the wheel turn without forcing the chain and pedals to move. It locks when the rider pedals forward.","anchor":"drivetrain"}
